1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,016
Runnable says do this. But what if the task produces a result?

2
00:00:04,016 --> 00:00:08,292
Callable is Runnable with a return value — and checked exceptions.

3
00:00:08,292 --> 00:00:12,568
Submit a Callable, get a Future — a handle to the eventual result.

4
00:00:12,568 --> 00:00:15,547
Block on get, cancel if needed, check if done.

5
00:00:15,547 --> 00:00:19,499
CompletableFuture takes it further — compose async pipelines.

6
00:00:19,499 --> 00:00:23,386
Today — Callable, Future, and an intro to CompletableFuture.

7
00:00:23,386 --> 00:00:24,923
Episode Forty-One.

8
00:00:24,923 --> 00:00:28,340
Callable, Future, and CompletableFuture.

9
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:32,716
Callable of T is a functional interface — T call throws Exception.

10
00:00:32,716 --> 00:00:37,158
Like Runnable but returns a value and can throw checked exceptions.

11
00:00:37,158 --> 00:00:41,733
Submit to an ExecutorService — the pool runs call on a worker thread.

12
00:00:41,733 --> 00:00:46,507
Use lambdas — Callable task equals open paren close paren arrow compute.

13
00:00:46,507 --> 00:00:51,281
Callable fits any task that produces a result — fetch, parse, calculate.

14
00:00:51,281 --> 00:00:54,198
Separate the computation from where it runs.

15
00:00:54,198 --> 00:00:58,592
Future of T represents a pending result of an asynchronous computation.

16
00:00:58,592 --> 00:01:02,615
get blocks until the result is ready — optionally with a timeout.

17
00:01:02,615 --> 00:01:06,948
get with timeout — wait up to a duration, then throw TimeoutException.

18
00:01:06,948 --> 00:01:11,094
isDone checks completion without blocking. cancel attempts to stop.

19
00:01:11,094 --> 00:01:15,241
cancel with mayInterruptIfRunning — true interrupts a running task.

20
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:19,264
Always handle ExecutionException — the real cause is in getCause.

21
00:01:19,264 --> 00:01:24,080
CompletableFuture of T — a Future you can compose and complete manually.

22
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:27,826
supplyAsync runs a supplier on the default ForkJoinPool.

23
00:01:27,826 --> 00:01:32,508
thenApply transforms the result. thenCompose chains dependent futures.

24
00:01:32,508 --> 00:01:35,251
allOf and anyOf combine multiple futures.

25
00:01:35,251 --> 00:01:38,395
exceptionally handles failures in the pipeline.

26
00:01:38,395 --> 00:01:43,010
CompletableFuture is the modern way to build async workflows in Java.

27
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:45,712
Runnable versus Callable versus Future.

28
00:01:45,712 --> 00:01:49,591
Runnable — void, no checked exceptions, fire-and-forget.

29
00:01:49,591 --> 00:01:53,955
Callable — returns T, throws Exception, submitted for a Future.

30
00:01:53,955 --> 00:01:57,003
Future — read-only view of a pending result.

31
00:01:57,003 --> 00:02:00,605
CompletableFuture — writable, composable, chainable.

32
00:02:00,605 --> 00:02:05,316
Choose based on whether you need a result and how you compose tasks.

33
00:02:05,316 --> 00:02:07,537
When to use Callable and Future.

34
00:02:07,537 --> 00:02:11,632
Parallel API calls — submit many, collect results with get.

35
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:15,657
CPU work off the request thread — return Future to caller.

36
00:02:15,657 --> 00:02:19,058
Batch processing where each unit produces output.

37
00:02:19,058 --> 00:02:23,639
CompletableFuture when you need chaining — thenApply, thenCombine.

38
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:28,150
When not — simple fire-and-forget — Runnable and execute suffice.

39
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,674
Three common mistakes.

40
00:02:29,674 --> 00:02:33,761
One — calling get on the event loop thread — blocks the UI.

41
00:02:33,761 --> 00:02:38,056
Two — ignoring ExecutionException — swallowing the real error.

42
00:02:38,056 --> 00:02:42,628
Three — not setting timeouts on get — waits forever on hung tasks.

43
00:02:42,628 --> 00:02:46,300
Also — chaining blocking gets instead of thenCompose.

44
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:51,080
Async code needs async thinking — do not block what should stay free.

45
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:54,273
Interview question — Callable versus Runnable?

46
00:02:54,273 --> 00:02:57,396
Runnable returns void, no checked exceptions.

47
00:02:57,396 --> 00:03:01,422
Callable returns a value and can throw checked exceptions.

48
00:03:01,422 --> 00:03:05,378
Submit Callable to ExecutorService — receive Future of T.

49
00:03:05,378 --> 00:03:09,334
Future get blocks for result — use timeout in production.

50
00:03:09,334 --> 00:03:13,290
Mention CompletableFuture for composable async pipelines.

51
00:03:13,290 --> 00:03:18,279
Tasks and futures coordinate work. What about shared data structures?

52
00:03:18,279 --> 00:03:21,388
Episode Forty-Two — Concurrent Collections.

53
00:03:21,388 --> 00:03:26,016
ConcurrentHashMap, CopyOnWriteArrayList, and thread-safe queues.

54
00:03:26,016 --> 00:03:27,028
See you there.
